    "updated_at": "2023-07-24T18:02:30Z",
    "body": "2023 Remarks:\r\n- neither [`<figure>`][def-figure] nor [`<blockquote>`][def-blockquote] seem to be [\"sectioning root\"][sectioning-root-2016] any more (there seems to be no such thing currently in the spec), so IIUC putting [`<footer>`][def-footer] inside either `blockquote` or `figure` means that the `footer` _still_ belongs to the [_closest `article`, `aside`, `nav`, or `section`_][def-sectioning-content] (i.e. element constituting \"sectioning content\"), so it is not related to (closely) enclosing `figure` or `blockquote`.  Right?\r\n- There seems to be some confusion which structure is currently more appropriate for marking up even the simplest block quotations:\r\n\r\nWhether to stick to **`blockquote > footer` (\"Old\" (\"W3C\" (?)) structure** that currently works with all user agents (but is not valid in a sense that, as was pointed out, the `blockquote` is not the scoping element):\r\n\r\n```HTML\r\n<blockquote>\r\n  <p>Words.</p>\r\n  <footer>Said the Author in <cite>The Work</cite>.</footer>\r\n</blockquote>\r\n ```\r\n\r\n…or **`figure > blockquote + figcaption` (\"new\"  (\"WHATWG\"(?)) structure**, that is [reportedly slightly broken in certain UAs][aardrians-mdn-report]).\r\n \r\n ```HTML\r\n<figure>\r\n  <blockquote>\r\n    <p>Words.</p>\r\n  </blockquote>\r\n  <figcaption>Said the Author in <cite>The Work</cite>.</figcaption>\r\n</figure>\r\n```\r\n\r\n[def-sectioning-content]: https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/dom.html#sectioning-content\r\n[def-footer]: https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/grouping-content.html#the-footer-element\r\n[def-blockquote]: https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/grouping-content.html#the-blockquote-element\r\n[def-figure]: https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/grouping-content.html#the-figure-element\r\n[sectioning-root-2016]: http://web.archive.org/web/20160803150624/https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/semantics.html#sectioning-root\r\n[aardrians-mdn-report]: https://github.com/mdn/interactive-examples/issues/2563",
